WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.940
Avengers: Endgame didn't simply hit the Disney+
content shelves like the hundreds of other

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.380
previously released, Disney-owned movies did.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.280
On the contrary, it showed up on the new streaming
service with a few added delights.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.300
Here's all the never-before-seen Endgame footage
revealed by Disney+.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:19.400
The death of Black Widow was one of Endgame's
most tragic moments.

00:00:19.409 --> 00:00:23.560
Watching Widow and her fellow hero Hawkeye
engage in an emotional tug-of-war over who

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:28.359
would sacrifice themselves to obtain the Soul
Stone was heartbreaking enough, but witnessing

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:32.580
Widow jump off that cliff and tell Hawkeye
to let her go was devastating.

00:00:32.829 --> 00:00:37.300
But it could have gone down a bit differently:
the deleted scenes available on Disney+ reveal

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:42.739
never-before-seen footage of Black Widow getting
shot by Thanos' Chitauri minions, who arrive

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:45.660
on Vormir and begin firing at her and Hawkeye.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:50.000
As she's running toward the cliff's edge,
Black Widow suffers several wounds, including

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.760
one to the torso that leaves her crawling
across the ground.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.440
In the end, she manages to turn around and
shoot an enemy who was about to kill Hawkeye,

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.200
then sacrifices herself as she does in the
standard cut of Endgame.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:06.660
A less-intense and unfinished deleted Endgame
scene bundled with Disney+ centers around

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:11.390
designing the silvery Quantum Realm suits
the heroes use during their time travel missions.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:16.780
In the scene, we watch as Tony Stark walks
into an area at Avengers HQ where Professor

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:20.049
Hulk is outfitting a crude CGI mannequin of
some sort.

00:01:20.049 --> 00:01:24.090
Iron Man inquires about the status of the
"thingamajigger," then admires how the Quantum

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:29.250
suit design blends technology made by Hank
Pym with "Stark styling" and a "noggin bubble"

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:33.320
courtesy of Nebula and her space-faring friends,
or, as Tony calls them,

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:34.360
"'Rings of Uranus?'

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:35.600
What's your troupe called?"

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.040
"The Guardians of the Galaxy."

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:41.900
When Professor Hulk states that someone will
have to test out the Quantum Realm suit, Ant-Man

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:46.800
says "not it!" before Hawkeye steps into the
scene and offers to take the suit for a spin.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:52.240
On Disney+, fans can also find two deleted
Endgame scenes focused on Bruce Banner and

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.861
The Ancient One, the leader of the Masters
of the Mystic Arts who explains to Banner

00:01:55.861 --> 00:01:59.940
how messing with the Infinity Stones can alter
reality if they aren't returned to the exact

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.880
moment in time from which they were taken.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:06.200
One sequence shows Hulk meeting with the Ancient
One, who's relaxing with a drink in her hand

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.090
and a pair of sunglasses on her face.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:12.440
In this cut, she explains to Hulk that he's
"five years too early," and that Doctor Strange

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.940
has no knowledge of the Time Stone for which
Hulk and the Avengers are searching.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:19.140
The deleted scene ends with Hulk asking who
the Ancient One is.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:23.180
The second deleted scene is an alternate take
of the time travel explanation sequence.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:27.260
Here, the Ancient One is speaking with Hulk
instead of Bruce Banner - evidence that she

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.190
didn't knock Banner's soul out of Professor
Hulk's body to better connect with him in

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:31.880
conversation.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:36.280
The discussion goes mostly the same as the
one seen in the theatrical cut of Endgame,

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.081
but the deleted scene included on Disney+
features the Ancient One admitting that she

00:02:40.081 --> 00:02:45.030
was aware of Thanos' potential for destruction
but didn't do anything about it, since taking

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:48.140
precautions with Thanos could have altered
something else in the universe.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.400
"Easy-peasy lemon squeezy."

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.000
"You're a very interesting person."

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:55.500
"It's quite a burden."

00:02:56.300 --> 00:03:01.260
Another never-before-seen Endgame moment revealed
on Disney+ is a scrapped scene that shows

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:05.940
Earth's Mightiest Heroes assembling in the
trenches during the epic battle against Thanos.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.100
As directors Joe and Anthony Russo explain
on the commentary track, the sequence was

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:14.370
meant to be a "building block" for the climax
of Endgame, but the Russos would up abandoning

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:18.890
the idea for a variety of reasons - namely
that the moment was missing narrative substance

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:20.400
and wasn't all that interesting.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:25.040
An off-shoot of this idea, the Russos note,
was to have this pep talk in the Mirror Dimension

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:29.320
- the parallel dimension in which practitioners
of magic can do things outside the public

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:29.820
eye.

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.020
"Easy-peasy lemon squeezy!"

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:37.500
The final additional scene snipped from Endgame
that's loaded onto Disney+ centers around

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:42.230
Tony Stark in the moments after snaps his
fingers, defeats Thanos and his army, saves

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:45.320
the universe, and sacrifices himself for the
greater good.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:50.340
Post-snap, he's transported to what Joe and
Anthony Russo refer to as "The Way Station"

00:03:50.349 --> 00:03:54.290
- the metaphysical location where Thanos himself
went after he killed his adopted daughter

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:57.290
Gamora to obtain the Soul Stone in Infinity
War.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:01.970
There, Tony meets a grown-up version of his
daughter, Morgan, played by 13 Reasons Why

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.460
actress Katherine Langford.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:08.000
At first, he doesn't recognize the young woman
he's speaking to - but when Morgan quips that

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:12.960
the two of them are "pretty close," Tony realizes
she's the same person who often told him she

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.820
"loved him 3,000" as a child.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:19.420
Morgan explains that her father's sacrifice
worked, that she got to live and grow up and

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:19.920
be happy.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:24.380
When Tony admits that he's scared he "made
a mistake," Morgan says she understands, but

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.600
she's very proud of him.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:28.340
She also assures her father that she's okay
without him:

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:29.940
"I'm strong, like Mom.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.100
And I'm happy.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:37.580
I'm happy we had the time that we did, and
that you were there for me - until you couldn't

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:38.080
be."

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:42.740
Of course, the scene wraps up the way all
scenes between Tony and Morgan Stark should:

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.280
"I love you 3,000."

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:48.880
According to the Russos, the "Tony in the
afterlife" scene didn't make it into Endgame

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.160
because it "felt like it ground the movie
to a halt."

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:55.640
It saved audiences a ton of tears as well,
but you didn't need the Russos to tell you

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:56.140
that.

